{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Found.</b> An anomalous word in grammar, for the tsadi ought to have a kamatz gadol, as in the example 'and the people found in the palace are his servants and his servants' servants.'" "<b>ביתן.</b> From the root בית, and it is in construct state and also pointed. Its meaning is like 'within,' and similarly 'inside and outside,' and it is a shortened form: ביתן [is] the king's house."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:37.683736189Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}